// The spawn director overhaul's balance bands (ARCHITECTURE §8 note 930; the director's brief,
// docs/design/spawn-director-overhaul.md §7 "Initial balance targets"): what `dt director report` scores a `dt director sweep`
// against, each group green inside its band and red outside. Benchmarks for simulation and playtesting, never spawn quotas
// (§7: "Do not hardcode these counts as spawn quotas"); nothing in the game reads this file.
//
// From the brief, as written (BalanceBandsTests pins them):
//   encounters: distinct meaningful encounters in a 20-minute night (the sweep's encountersPer20Min), by session. A group is
//     judged by the first session whose crew it has and whose cars range holds its train; a group no session holds isn't.
//   firstThreatSeconds: "First noticeable threat generally occurs within 90-150 seconds after leaving the safe departure
//     area" (the sweep's firstThreat, counted from the night's grace).
//   lateAtLeastEarly: "Encounters become measurably more frequent toward the latter half of the night".
//
// Ours, where the brief says what to watch but gives no number (the director's to change; note 930):
//   droughtsOver90: "Investigate ordinary mid-run stretches exceeding 90 seconds without a meaningful threat": at most this
//     many a night, on the mean.
//   deliveredAtLeast: "Do not force these targets at the expense of basic playability, travel time, or the ability to
//     finish runs": the share of a group's nights that get home.
{
  "encounters": [
    { "crew": 1, "cars": [2, 3], "per20Min": [5, 8] },
    { "crew": 2, "cars": [4, 6], "per20Min": [7, 11] },
    { "crew": 4, "cars": [8, 8], "per20Min": [10, 15] },
    { "crew": 8, "cars": [12, 99], "per20Min": [14, 20] }
  ],
  "firstThreatSeconds": [90, 150],
  "lateAtLeastEarly": true,
  "droughtsOver90": 2,
  "deliveredAtLeast": 0.75
}
